Optional plugins (separate downloads) keep their own licenses, e.g. the
NVIDIA driver plugin (NVIDIA license terms for the user-space libraries).
From v0.1.0-beta.2 the separate NVIDIA plugin includes open kernel modules
(MIT/GPL-2.0), NVIDIA-licensed user-space libraries/GSP firmware and NVIDIA
Container Toolkit (Apache-2.0). Its release assets include matching kernel
sources and a separate original-license archive with pinned package URLs.
See docs/NVIDIA.md. Firmware may be binary-only;
a Debian source-package link does not imply availability of firmware source code.

Development builds also provide Intel GPU Tools as a separate Debian-based
plugin (mainly MIT, plus licenses of included libraries). Its licenses archive
includes original Debian copyright notices and exact source-package URLs in
usr/share/titanos/intel-gpu-tools/SOURCES.txt. The Coral USB helper is TitanOS
code under FSL-1.1-ALv2. No Google libedgetpu binary or firmware is bundled;
a container application must supply its own appropriately licensed runtime.

Tailscale plugin: Tailscale 1.104.1, BSD-3-Clause, plus third-party components
under their original licenses. The plugin and tailscale-licenses.tar.gz include
the upstream license and dependency notices from https://tailscale.com/licenses/tailscale.
Source: https://github.com/tailscale/tailscale/tree/v1.104.1
NetBird plugin: NetBird client 0.81.5, BSD-3-Clause, plus Go modules under their
original licenses (MIT, BSD, Apache-2.0, ISC, MPL-2.0 and others). Only the client
is shipped; NetBird's AGPL-3.0 server components are not included. The plugin and
netbird-licenses.tar.gz include the upstream LICENSE and the notices of every
linked module with one source link each (third-party.txt).
Source: https://github.com/netbirdio/netbird/tree/v0.81.5
NVIDIA build SDK: Debian build tools and exact kernel headers retain their original
licenses. Its archive includes package notices; nvidia-build-sdk-sources.txt lists
the corresponding Debian source packages. The SDK is separate from the NAS RAM image.
